"Let $T$ be an oriented tree, let $n=|V(T)|$ be its order, and let $\\operatorname{unvd}(T)$ denote its unavoidability.\n\n**Sumner's conjecture.** Every oriented tree of order $n>1$ is $(2n-2)$-unavoidable; equivalently,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{unvd}(T)\\leqslant 2n-2.\n$$\n\nThis is a celebrated conjecture about tournaments and oriented trees. The source does not state a resolution, so its status remains open."